00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:33,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:00,667 --> 00:00:02,233
What did Sota say?

2
00:00:02,333 --> 00:00:03,333
He said he's sorry...

3
00:00:03,367 --> 00:00:04,367
Silver anniversary?

4
00:00:04,433 --> 00:00:05,993
Can you keep it a secret until the end?

5
00:00:06,033 --> 00:00:08,567
I know for sure that I like you.

6
00:00:09,167 --> 00:00:09,533
Huh?

7
00:00:09,633 --> 00:00:13,467
But I still don't know
exactly what kind of 'like' this is.

8
00:00:13,567 --> 00:00:16,300
Will you help me figure it out?

9
00:00:16,733 --> 00:00:17,733
Yeah.

10
00:00:17,967 --> 00:00:19,287
I want to figure it out with you.

11
00:00:25,833 --> 00:00:27,033
Oh, right.

12
00:00:27,667 --> 00:00:28,667
What is it?

13
00:00:28,733 --> 00:00:31,173
The mock exam results come
out the day after tomorrow, right?

14
00:00:31,567 --> 00:00:32,600
Come on.

15
00:00:33,167 --> 00:00:35,533
I guess I'm the only one excited about it.

16
00:00:35,633 --> 00:00:36,633
Well, yeah.

17
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,860
Do you have any plans
for the day after tomorrow?

18
00:00:39,933 --> 00:00:41,133
Not really.

19
00:00:43,733 --> 00:00:44,733
If...

20
00:00:45,433 --> 00:00:46,167
Uh...

21
00:00:46,267 --> 00:00:46,667
You go first.

22
00:00:46,767 --> 00:00:48,833
No, you go ahead.

23
00:00:49,333 --> 00:00:50,333
Well then...

24
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:53,267
If I get a grade E or
higher on the mock exam...

25
00:00:53,367 --> 00:00:54,367
Ah.

26
00:00:54,833 --> 00:00:56,993
(Did a great job)
Then you'll have collected 20 stickers.

27
00:00:57,133 --> 00:00:58,200
Can I claim my reward?

28
00:00:58,300 --> 00:00:58,767
Of course.

29
00:00:58,867 --> 00:00:59,867
What do you want?

30
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:01,867
I'm not telling you yet.

31
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:03,467
Huh? I want to know right now.

32
00:01:03,567 --> 00:01:04,167
No way.

33
00:01:04,267 --> 00:01:06,333
Wow, so stingy.

34
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:07,800
What about you?

35
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:09,180
What were you going to say?

36
00:01:09,767 --> 00:01:10,767
Oh.

37
00:01:11,567 --> 00:01:12,567
Well...

38
00:01:13,067 --> 00:01:14,067
I was going to say...

39
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:16,460
If the weather is nice tomorrow...

40
00:01:16,633 --> 00:01:20,167
Should we wash the sheets?

41
00:01:20,867 --> 00:01:22,600
Come on, so that's what it was.

42
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:23,533
You know.

43
00:01:23,633 --> 00:01:26,567
We've been having a lot of
afternoon showers lately, right?

44
00:01:28,200 --> 00:01:29,500
Hey...

45
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:31,167
What are you even talking about?

46
00:01:31,267 --> 00:01:34,400
I really wanted us to celebrate together.

47
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:37,167
I was just way too nervous.

48
00:01:37,267 --> 00:01:39,733
Na-chan seemed as normal as ever.

49
00:01:40,333 --> 00:01:41,533
That's impressive.

50
00:01:41,867 --> 00:01:43,133
True.

51
00:01:43,233 --> 00:01:45,273
Tomorrow might actually
be a great day for laundry.

52
00:01:45,667 --> 00:01:46,667
Yeah.

53
00:01:47,333 --> 00:01:48,500
But...

54
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:50,767
This feeling of nothing changing...

55
00:01:51,567 --> 00:01:53,700
This feeling of everything
being the same as usual...

56
00:01:55,167 --> 00:01:56,700
Somehow...

57
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:58,267
It's actually pretty nice.

58
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:09,967
"Your Summer, My Storm"
(Episode 8)

59
00:02:16,267 --> 00:02:17,867
Huh, isn't that great?

60
00:02:18,033 --> 00:02:20,367
Wanting to figure out
what kind of 'like' it is.

61
00:02:20,767 --> 00:02:22,233
That's wonderful. It's very Sota.

62
00:02:23,233 --> 00:02:24,233
Yeah.

63
00:02:24,767 --> 00:02:25,767
Wait.

64
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,167
Huh? What's wrong?

65
00:02:27,267 --> 00:02:28,809
That expression you just made was great.

66
00:02:28,833 --> 00:02:29,400
What?

67
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:32,233
Natsuki actually looked kind of cute.

68
00:02:32,733 --> 00:02:33,893
What's that supposed to mean?

69
00:02:33,933 --> 00:02:34,833
What was that look just now?

70
00:02:34,933 --> 00:02:36,109
- What?
- Come on, do it again.

71
00:02:36,133 --> 00:02:37,943
- No, I don't want to.
- Show me one more time.

72
00:02:37,967 --> 00:02:38,667
Ah.

73
00:02:38,767 --> 00:02:40,500
Oh, it's Fuku-chan.

74
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:41,467
That was a fast reply.

75
00:02:41,567 --> 00:02:42,667
Yeah.

76
00:02:42,767 --> 00:02:43,667
Hello.

77
00:02:43,767 --> 00:02:44,833
Fuku-chan.

78
00:02:44,933 --> 00:02:46,367
You're both here.

79
00:02:46,467 --> 00:02:47,267
Did you see the message?

80
00:02:47,367 --> 00:02:47,967
I did.

81
00:02:48,067 --> 00:02:49,843
Are things really that
tense with your folks?

82
00:02:49,867 --> 00:02:50,500
Yeah.

83
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:52,633
The atmosphere at home is terrible.

84
00:02:55,067 --> 00:02:55,900
Well...

85
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,667
I really can't stand watching it anymore.

86
00:02:58,633 --> 00:03:00,533
Then we need to come up with a plan fast.

87
00:03:00,633 --> 00:03:01,633
Right?

88
00:03:02,133 --> 00:03:03,443
Instead of waiting for their anniversary...

89
00:03:03,467 --> 00:03:06,500
How about we throw a surprise
party early and just reveal it?

90
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:07,680
I think that's a good idea.

91
00:03:07,767 --> 00:03:08,400
Let's do that.

92
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:08,967
Oh.

93
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:10,167
Then it's decided.

94
00:03:10,267 --> 00:03:11,867
So, who should we invite?

95
00:03:11,967 --> 00:03:14,500
Hmm... The three of us.

96
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:15,133
Yeah.

97
00:03:15,233 --> 00:03:17,333
And Mayumi-san and Kaoru-san?

98
00:03:17,433 --> 00:03:19,133
Oh, and Riku and Yanagi-san.

99
00:03:19,233 --> 00:03:20,433
Yeah, sounds good.

100
00:03:20,833 --> 00:03:22,167
And also...

101
00:03:22,767 --> 00:03:23,900
Sota.

102
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:25,000
Huh?

103
00:03:25,167 --> 00:03:25,900
Hmm?

104
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,800
Well, I think that's a great idea.

105
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:29,400
Ah.

106
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:32,033
Then... I'll go ask if he's free.

107
00:03:32,367 --> 00:03:33,167
So...

108
00:03:33,267 --> 00:03:35,200
What should I prepare?

109
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:37,567
Hmm... As for Fuku-chan...

110
00:03:38,633 --> 00:03:39,633
Huh?

111
00:03:40,433 --> 00:03:42,933
(When My Son Falls for a Man)

112
00:03:43,133 --> 00:03:46,567
You're in charge of covering
for us so Mom doesn't catch on.

113
00:03:46,667 --> 00:03:48,767
- Yeah.
- Covering for you guys with Mom, got it.

114
00:03:49,467 --> 00:03:50,567
Leave it to me.

115
00:03:55,433 --> 00:03:56,767
Three minutes left.

116
00:03:56,867 --> 00:03:58,376
Are the mock exam
results really that exciting?

117
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:00,433
I just feel depressed about it.

118
00:04:00,533 --> 00:04:02,767
Why don't you just ask
Sota-san to tutor you too, Ryo?

119
00:04:02,867 --> 00:04:04,033
No can do.

120
00:04:04,133 --> 00:04:05,133
Hmm?

121
00:04:05,833 --> 00:04:06,867
Ah.

122
00:04:06,967 --> 00:04:08,133
So-chan is really busy.

123
00:04:08,233 --> 00:04:09,067
- Yeah.
- That's true.

124
00:04:09,167 --> 00:04:10,367
Besides...

125
00:04:10,467 --> 00:04:13,167
If I'm getting a tutor, it
has to be a college girl.

126
00:04:13,267 --> 00:04:14,409
You're disqualified for
having ulterior motives.

127
00:04:14,433 --> 00:04:15,673
- Disqualified?
- Ah, it's here.

128
00:04:15,733 --> 00:04:16,567
- Huh?
- How are your results?

129
00:04:16,667 --> 00:04:18,367
How did you do?

130
00:04:25,700 --> 00:04:29,067
(Study Abroad Brochure)

131
00:04:32,267 --> 00:04:33,433
What's this?

132
00:04:33,533 --> 00:04:35,267
Are you already job hunting?

133
00:04:35,700 --> 00:04:37,767
I don't want to think about that so soon.

134
00:04:37,867 --> 00:04:38,500
Well...

135
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:40,000
Pretty much.

136
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:42,500
Let me enjoy my
college life a little longer.

137
00:04:47,033 --> 00:04:48,433
(New message from Na-chan)

138
00:04:49,700 --> 00:04:50,700
(It's a C)

139
00:04:50,767 --> 00:04:51,133
Huh?

140
00:04:51,233 --> 00:04:51,933
Oh.

141
00:04:52,033 --> 00:04:54,267
Wow, that's great!

142
00:04:54,733 --> 00:04:56,000
Hey.

143
00:04:56,233 --> 00:04:57,733
Wow, that's really amazing.

144
00:04:57,833 --> 00:04:59,133
Heh.

145
00:04:59,233 --> 00:05:00,733
That's great.

146
00:05:00,833 --> 00:05:01,567
(Grade C)
Huh?

147
00:05:01,667 --> 00:05:02,500
(Grade C)
Wow, that's impressive.

148
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:04,433
That's really impressive.

149
00:05:04,533 --> 00:05:06,733
Not bad, you skipped D
and went straight to a C.

150
00:05:06,833 --> 00:05:08,376
I told you I could do it
if I got serious.

151
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:09,133
(Kobayakawa Sota)
Yeah.

152
00:05:09,233 --> 00:05:10,300
I couldn't tell.

153
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:11,400
Ah.

154
00:05:15,133 --> 00:05:16,133
Hello.

155
00:05:17,733 --> 00:05:19,900
Na-chan, you're amazing.

156
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:24,700
And I actually got a 75 in math.

157
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,033
Seriously?

158
00:05:26,133 --> 00:05:27,967
That's incredible, so awesome.

159
00:05:29,233 --> 00:05:30,233
And also...

160
00:05:30,967 --> 00:05:33,267
Can I claim my sticker reward?

161
00:05:33,367 --> 00:05:34,133
Yeah.

162
00:05:34,233 --> 00:05:35,133
Of course.

163
00:05:35,233 --> 00:05:36,400
What do you want?

164
00:05:36,967 --> 00:05:37,967
Well...

165
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:40,000
I want to go out and have fun.

166
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,000
Huh?

167
00:05:43,267 --> 00:05:44,633
With So-chan.

168
00:05:50,333 --> 00:05:51,333
Yeah.

169
00:05:51,567 --> 00:05:52,933
Let's go out.

170
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:53,900
Yeah.

171
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,067
Okay.

172
00:05:59,967 --> 00:06:02,267
Make sure you thank him properly.

173
00:06:02,367 --> 00:06:02,900
Yeah.

174
00:06:03,333 --> 00:06:04,533
Say hi to Sota for me.

175
00:06:04,633 --> 00:06:05,233
Yeah.

176
00:06:05,333 --> 00:06:06,400
I'm heading out.

177
00:06:06,500 --> 00:06:07,967
Take care.

178
00:06:37,733 --> 00:06:39,733
Na-chan.

179
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:49,000
Congratulations.

180
00:06:50,267 --> 00:06:51,733
You really worked hard.

181
00:06:52,633 --> 00:06:54,509
It's not like I passed the
college entrance exam.

182
00:06:54,533 --> 00:06:56,333
Who cares? Just let me congratulate you.

183
00:06:56,900 --> 00:06:58,467
Yeah, I guess.

184
00:06:58,567 --> 00:06:59,633
Let's have a blast today.

185
00:06:59,733 --> 00:07:01,300
- Yeah.
- What do you want to do?

186
00:07:02,267 --> 00:07:04,400
I want to do the things
So-chan usually does.

187
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:05,500
Huh?

188
00:07:07,733 --> 00:07:08,167
Okay.

189
00:07:08,267 --> 00:07:09,267
So-chan.

190
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:12,267
Not bad.

191
00:07:12,367 --> 00:07:13,267
You look like a pro.

192
00:07:13,367 --> 00:07:14,033
Cool, right?

193
00:07:14,133 --> 00:07:14,767
Yeah.

194
00:07:14,867 --> 00:07:15,867
Well then...

195
00:07:15,967 --> 00:07:16,567
Let's get started.

196
00:07:16,667 --> 00:07:17,167
Yeah.

197
00:07:17,333 --> 00:07:19,633
You grip it from the top, like this.

198
00:07:19,733 --> 00:07:20,500
Grip it from the top, like this.

199
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:21,500
Then lift it up.

200
00:07:21,600 --> 00:07:22,600
Lift it up.

201
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:24,800
Alright, let's start with
some practice swings.

202
00:07:24,900 --> 00:07:26,367
Like this.

203
00:07:26,467 --> 00:07:27,467
Swing it out.

204
00:07:27,733 --> 00:07:29,467
Like this... swing it out.

205
00:07:29,567 --> 00:07:31,067
You need to relax a bit more.

206
00:07:31,167 --> 00:07:33,267
I know, like this... swing it out.

207
00:07:33,367 --> 00:07:34,433
Huh?

208
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:40,333
Oh...

209
00:07:40,433 --> 00:07:41,200
Something like that.

210
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:42,467
Okay.

211
00:07:42,567 --> 00:07:43,567
Alright.

212
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,233
Shoot.

213
00:07:46,333 --> 00:07:47,533
So close.

214
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:49,133
Tennis is pretty tough, huh?

215
00:07:49,233 --> 00:07:50,909
It's always like this when
you're just starting out.

216
00:07:50,933 --> 00:07:51,767
Okay, let's try again.

217
00:07:51,867 --> 00:07:52,533
Yeah.

218
00:07:52,633 --> 00:07:53,633
Alright.

219
00:07:54,367 --> 00:07:55,367
Swing.

220
00:07:57,300 --> 00:08:01,400
I thought you'd pick up
a sport like this in no time.

221
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:02,633
Who would've thought?

222
00:08:02,733 --> 00:08:03,400
What?

223
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:05,109
I'll get the hang of
it once I'm used to it.

224
00:08:05,133 --> 00:08:06,133
Here it comes.

225
00:08:07,367 --> 00:08:08,100
Almost.

226
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:08,667
Alright.

227
00:08:08,767 --> 00:08:09,833
- Ah, so close.
- Yeah.

228
00:08:09,933 --> 00:08:11,733
Keep your eyes on the ball.

229
00:08:12,367 --> 00:08:14,100
Plant your feet, aim, and then hit.

230
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,533
Watch it closely.

231
00:08:15,633 --> 00:08:16,633
Here.

232
00:08:17,167 --> 00:08:17,933
Nice.

233
00:08:18,033 --> 00:08:19,333
That's the feeling.

234
00:08:20,167 --> 00:08:20,800
Here.

235
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:21,533
Wait.

236
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:21,967
You got this.

237
00:08:22,067 --> 00:08:23,400
Run to it, stop, then hit.

238
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:24,300
Right...

239
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:25,433
Next one's over here.

240
00:08:25,533 --> 00:08:26,700
Run to it, stop.

241
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:27,467
Good.

242
00:08:27,567 --> 00:08:28,567
Don't look away.

243
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:30,533
Nice shot.

244
00:08:30,633 --> 00:08:31,433
Stop before you swing.

245
00:08:31,533 --> 00:08:32,333
Stop, then swing.

246
00:08:32,433 --> 00:08:33,767
Yeah, you're getting better.

247
00:08:34,033 --> 00:08:35,033
Here.

248
00:08:35,333 --> 00:08:36,333
Huh?

249
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:36,867
Here.

250
00:08:36,967 --> 00:08:37,967
Great shot.

251
00:08:38,133 --> 00:08:38,900
Oops.

252
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:40,233
This is starting to get fun.

253
00:08:41,633 --> 00:08:42,333
Right?

254
00:08:42,433 --> 00:08:43,433
Yeah.

255
00:08:54,967 --> 00:08:56,000
Um... Mom.

256
00:08:56,100 --> 00:08:56,667
Hmm?

257
00:08:56,767 --> 00:08:57,767
What's wrong?

258
00:08:58,133 --> 00:08:59,133
Uh...

259
00:08:59,400 --> 00:09:01,167
It's about Natsuki...

260
00:09:02,433 --> 00:09:03,433
Yeah.

261
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:07,133
You've already figured it out, haven't you?

262
00:09:08,167 --> 00:09:09,767
About the person Natsuki likes.

263
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:12,467
Huh?

264
00:09:12,933 --> 00:09:15,433
Natsuki has a crush on someone?

265
00:09:22,467 --> 00:09:23,467
A while ago...

266
00:09:24,133 --> 00:09:25,800
I accidentally saw it.

267
00:09:27,433 --> 00:09:28,867
On your computer.

268
00:09:30,333 --> 00:09:31,333
Huh?

269
00:09:32,667 --> 00:09:37,067
I saw that interview article,
'When My Son Falls for a Man.'

270
00:09:38,633 --> 00:09:40,153
The screen was left open on that page.

271
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:43,033
Ah...

272
00:09:43,967 --> 00:09:45,367
Don't tell me...

273
00:09:45,467 --> 00:09:48,700
Did you overhear my
conversation with Natsuki?

274
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:54,700
Yeah.

275
00:09:56,867 --> 00:09:58,200
I knew it...

276
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:08,567
Ah... I'm exhausted.

277
00:10:08,667 --> 00:10:09,400
Tired?

278
00:10:09,500 --> 00:10:10,300
Yeah.

279
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:12,367
I really underestimated tennis.

280
00:10:12,467 --> 00:10:14,167
It might be just as exhausting as soccer.

281
00:10:15,467 --> 00:10:17,033
But you're pretty good, Na-chan.

282
00:10:17,133 --> 00:10:18,833
You've got a lot of room to grow.

283
00:10:18,933 --> 00:10:19,533
Right?

284
00:10:19,633 --> 00:10:20,633
Yeah.

285
00:10:20,900 --> 00:10:22,900
I feel like I could beat you next time.

286
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:23,767
Oh, really?

287
00:10:23,867 --> 00:10:24,933
I'm not going to lose.

288
00:10:25,033 --> 00:10:26,800
No, I've got room to grow.

289
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:28,533
No, I've got experience.

290
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:30,500
Ah.

291
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:32,000
Let's play soccer next time too.

292
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:35,100
Ah, that's a bit...

293
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:35,767
Ah.

294
00:10:36,167 --> 00:10:36,967
You're not good at it, huh?

295
00:10:37,067 --> 00:10:39,700
Well, I wouldn't exactly
say I'm good at it.

296
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:41,067
It's fine, I'll teach you.

297
00:10:41,167 --> 00:10:43,067
Huh, I feel like you'd lose your temper.

298
00:10:43,167 --> 00:10:43,700
What?

299
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:44,567
I wouldn't lose my temper
over something like that.

300
00:10:44,667 --> 00:10:45,833
Aren't you already losing it?

301
00:10:45,933 --> 00:10:46,933
No, I'm not.

302
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:47,600
You totally are.

303
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:48,167
Am not.

304
00:10:48,267 --> 00:10:49,267
Sounds like you are.

305
00:10:51,533 --> 00:10:52,973
You must have been really surprised.

306
00:10:53,567 --> 00:10:56,667
After all, times are different
from your generation.

307
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:00,967
Is Natsuki doing okay?

308
00:11:03,167 --> 00:11:04,167
What do you mean?

309
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:06,700
He gathered the courage to confess,

310
00:11:07,533 --> 00:11:09,500
but ended up getting rejected, right?

311
00:11:10,767 --> 00:11:11,767
Ah...

312
00:11:11,867 --> 00:11:13,133
Being rejected like that,

313
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,200
he must be really hurt.

314
00:11:16,900 --> 00:11:17,900
Ah.

315
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,733
- Mom, listen to me...
- And yet,

316
00:11:20,133 --> 00:11:22,733
he's still pretending to
be so strong and cheerful.

317
00:11:23,333 --> 00:11:24,367
Uh...

318
00:11:24,467 --> 00:11:25,200
He's really fine.

319
00:11:25,300 --> 00:11:27,133
How could he be fine?

320
00:11:27,233 --> 00:11:30,067
He even went out of his
way to tell me about it today.

321
00:11:31,067 --> 00:11:32,900
It breaks my heart.

322
00:11:34,500 --> 00:11:36,867
The reason he thought he was rejected

323
00:11:36,967 --> 00:11:38,247
was actually a misunderstanding.

324
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:40,700
Huh?

325
00:11:45,267 --> 00:11:48,233
At first, Sota was troubled too,

326
00:11:49,567 --> 00:11:51,400
but he's taking this very seriously.

327
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:58,133
Mom?

328
00:12:03,433 --> 00:12:04,433
Thank goodness...

329
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,233
I thought...

330
00:12:10,133 --> 00:12:12,567
that child was hurt.

331
00:12:14,867 --> 00:12:16,033
But...

332
00:12:16,133 --> 00:12:18,167
That's not the case, right?

333
00:12:21,033 --> 00:12:22,300
Thank goodness...

334
00:12:35,067 --> 00:12:36,167
Rio?

335
00:12:40,633 --> 00:12:41,733
Because...

336
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:44,667
What's wrong?

337
00:12:48,533 --> 00:12:50,933
I thought...

338
00:12:52,967 --> 00:12:55,233
you might look at Natsuki differently
because of this.

339
00:12:55,333 --> 00:12:57,833
How could I ever do that?

340
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:03,433
I'm sorry.

341
00:13:09,400 --> 00:13:10,433
Rio.

342
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:12,400
Thank you.

343
00:13:13,667 --> 00:13:15,067
I should be thanking you too.

344
00:13:16,367 --> 00:13:18,067
This is still a bit embarrassing.

345
00:13:18,667 --> 00:13:21,133
Weren't you the one who
wanted to take a picture?

346
00:13:21,333 --> 00:13:22,400
Well, yeah.

347
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:24,233
Alright, I'm taking it.

348
00:13:24,333 --> 00:13:25,576
- Let's do it.
- Huh, are we starting?

349
00:13:25,600 --> 00:13:26,667
Strike a good pose.

350
00:13:26,767 --> 00:13:27,200
Ah, I messed up.

351
00:13:27,300 --> 00:13:28,300
Definitely too slow.

352
00:13:28,367 --> 00:13:28,833
Here we go.

353
00:13:28,933 --> 00:13:29,733
Like this.

354
00:13:29,833 --> 00:13:30,367
Looks great.

355
00:13:30,467 --> 00:13:31,547
- Yay.
- Does it look great?

356
00:13:31,967 --> 00:13:32,767
- Huh, wait.
- Does it look great?

357
00:13:32,867 --> 00:13:35,367
I'm not even smiling.

358
00:13:35,467 --> 00:13:39,200
I almost started hating Sota-san.

359
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:40,300
Huh?

360
00:13:40,433 --> 00:13:42,367
I couldn't tell at all.

361
00:13:42,699 --> 00:13:45,766
I was thinking, 'Unforgivable,
hurting Natsuki like that.'

362
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,067
I see.

363
00:13:48,167 --> 00:13:49,067
Yeah.

364
00:13:49,167 --> 00:13:49,933
But,

365
00:13:50,033 --> 00:13:52,667
I was a bit worried back then too.

366
00:13:52,767 --> 00:13:53,767
You were too?

367
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:54,433
Yeah.

368
00:13:54,767 --> 00:13:57,367
I really didn't know what to do.

369
00:13:57,700 --> 00:13:59,433
I even went and asked the computer.

370
00:13:59,533 --> 00:14:00,667
Ah, you asked AI, right?

371
00:14:00,767 --> 00:14:01,667
I asked too.

372
00:14:01,767 --> 00:14:02,367
Really?

373
00:14:02,467 --> 00:14:02,900
Yeah.

374
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,100
It always told me it understood how I felt.

375
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:07,409
It empathized with my feelings,
which really put me at ease.

376
00:14:07,433 --> 00:14:08,700
I know, right?

377
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:11,700
No matter when,
it's always there to help you.

378
00:14:12,267 --> 00:14:13,267
Huh.

379
00:14:13,467 --> 00:14:15,667
Was it that nice to you too?

380
00:14:15,767 --> 00:14:16,333
Huh?

381
00:14:16,433 --> 00:14:17,133
Wait a minute.

382
00:14:17,233 --> 00:14:19,300
Mom, why are you getting jealous?

383
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:20,833
Uh, because...

384
00:14:23,733 --> 00:14:24,567
Huh.

385
00:14:24,667 --> 00:14:26,233
You can bring dogs here.

386
00:14:26,333 --> 00:14:27,133
Yeah.

387
00:14:27,233 --> 00:14:28,233
Ah.

388
00:14:28,333 --> 00:14:30,033
Let's bring Rock next time.

389
00:14:30,133 --> 00:14:31,133
Sure.

390
00:14:31,267 --> 00:14:34,233
I wonder if Rock would enjoy it.

391
00:14:34,333 --> 00:14:36,067
You've completely turned into a dog lover.

392
00:14:36,167 --> 00:14:36,700
Yeah.

393
00:14:36,867 --> 00:14:38,367
Because Rock is just so cute.

394
00:14:49,867 --> 00:14:50,733
Delicious.

395
00:14:50,833 --> 00:14:51,833
Yeah.

396
00:14:52,067 --> 00:14:53,367
It's so good.

397
00:14:53,467 --> 00:14:54,867
This place is seriously amazing.

398
00:14:54,967 --> 00:14:56,367
Yeah, I'm glad.

399
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:58,400
Do you come here often?

400
00:14:58,433 --> 00:14:59,300
Yeah.

401
00:14:59,400 --> 00:15:01,467
I come with Rio.

402
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:02,933
And Uesugi, too.

403
00:15:04,100 --> 00:15:04,700
Uesugi?

404
00:15:05,033 --> 00:15:05,600
Yeah.

405
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:06,900
He's in my class.

406
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,667
And in the same tennis club.

407
00:15:08,767 --> 00:15:09,767
Oh...

408
00:15:10,333 --> 00:15:12,633
Is he... a guy?

409
00:15:12,733 --> 00:15:13,733
Yeah.

410
00:15:14,367 --> 00:15:15,400
I see...

411
00:15:16,167 --> 00:15:17,167
Is that so?

412
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:19,800
Ah.

413
00:15:20,367 --> 00:15:22,967
Are you worried?

414
00:15:23,867 --> 00:15:24,400
Yeah.

415
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:26,167
I just feel a bit uneasy.

416
00:15:26,267 --> 00:15:26,900
Ah.

417
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,867
I'll introduce you to Uesugi next time.

418
00:15:28,967 --> 00:15:31,533
Then you'll see
there's no need to be jealous of him.

419
00:15:31,633 --> 00:15:32,467
Huh? Jealous?

420
00:15:32,567 --> 00:15:33,033
Hmm?

421
00:15:33,467 --> 00:15:34,267
Aren't you?

422
00:15:34,367 --> 00:15:35,733
Huh?

423
00:15:36,400 --> 00:15:37,400
- Huh?
- Ah.

424
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:39,300
I see.

425
00:15:39,967 --> 00:15:42,033
So this is what jealousy feels like.

426
00:15:44,567 --> 00:15:45,567
Huh...

427
00:15:46,333 --> 00:15:47,767
I see.

428
00:15:49,033 --> 00:15:50,300
So that's what it is.

429
00:15:50,400 --> 00:15:51,667
Makes sense.

430
00:15:53,833 --> 00:15:54,967
Na-chan.

431
00:15:55,067 --> 00:15:56,500
You're pretty funny.

432
00:15:56,667 --> 00:15:57,167
Huh?

433
00:15:57,267 --> 00:15:57,967
Are you making fun of me?

434
00:15:58,067 --> 00:15:59,700
No, I'm not.

435
00:15:59,933 --> 00:16:01,200
You totally are.

436
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:03,143
- I'm not.
- You're definitely making fun of me.

437
00:16:03,167 --> 00:16:04,400
Ah, it's Rock.

438
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:05,500
Huh?

439
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:06,600
No way.

440
00:16:07,333 --> 00:16:08,433
You stole my fries.

441
00:16:08,533 --> 00:16:09,400
I didn't.

442
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:10,567
You definitely did.

443
00:16:10,667 --> 00:16:12,167
By the way, So-chan.

444
00:16:12,267 --> 00:16:12,600
Hmm?

445
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:13,933
Are you busy this Sunday?

446
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:15,500
Huh?

447
00:16:18,633 --> 00:16:19,933
Oh...

448
00:16:20,033 --> 00:16:21,033
Huh?

449
00:16:21,433 --> 00:16:22,300
- Huh?
- Watch this.

450
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:23,633
Where should we hang this?

451
00:16:23,733 --> 00:16:24,567
- Riku, don't mess around.
- Hey!

452
00:16:24,667 --> 00:16:26,543
- Riku, don't mess around.
- It feels like something's missing.

453
00:16:26,567 --> 00:16:27,567
Ah.

454
00:16:28,167 --> 00:16:29,167
Olive oil.

455
00:16:29,233 --> 00:16:30,233
Geez.

456
00:16:33,333 --> 00:16:34,333
Riku.

457
00:16:35,133 --> 00:16:36,133
No snacking.

458
00:16:37,133 --> 00:16:38,800
But I want to eat it!

459
00:16:38,900 --> 00:16:40,267
Look.

460
00:16:40,367 --> 00:16:42,567
Even Rock is being patient.

461
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:43,767
Ah.

462
00:16:43,867 --> 00:16:45,143
Natsuki, a little more to the right.

463
00:16:45,167 --> 00:16:45,900
- Okay.
- A bit more.

464
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,300
No, that's the left.

465
00:16:49,167 --> 00:16:51,133
Sota, come help out too.

466
00:16:51,233 --> 00:16:52,233
Okay.

467
00:16:59,733 --> 00:17:01,667
Look, it looks so weird.

468
00:17:01,767 --> 00:17:03,300
Everyone, hurry up.

469
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:05,633
Mom and Dad will be back in half an hour.

470
00:17:06,533 --> 00:17:07,533
Achoo!

471
00:17:09,067 --> 00:17:09,767
Careful.

472
00:17:09,867 --> 00:17:10,867
Don't rush.

473
00:17:10,900 --> 00:17:12,800
Haste makes waste, as they say.

474
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:13,733
So-chan...

475
00:17:13,833 --> 00:17:15,300
Hand me that.

476
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:16,700
Yeah, that one.

477
00:17:16,800 --> 00:17:17,567
This one?

478
00:17:17,667 --> 00:17:18,167
That one.

479
00:17:18,267 --> 00:17:19,733
Just like Rock.

480
00:17:21,200 --> 00:17:24,333
It's because you couldn't make up
your mind, Fuku-chan. I'm exhausted.

481
00:17:24,433 --> 00:17:25,967
Oh, you really saved me.

482
00:17:26,067 --> 00:17:28,933
I had no idea what to buy
as a gift for my female subordinate.

483
00:17:29,033 --> 00:17:31,000
But I'm glad we found something nice.

484
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:32,100
Yeah.

485
00:17:32,667 --> 00:17:33,533
Ah, Uncle.

486
00:17:33,633 --> 00:17:36,167
Good work today.

487
00:17:36,267 --> 00:17:37,367
Welcome back.

488
00:17:38,733 --> 00:17:39,767
I'm home.

489
00:17:43,033 --> 00:17:45,000
You two are back.

490
00:17:46,333 --> 00:17:46,733
Come on in.

491
00:17:46,833 --> 00:17:47,833
What's going on?

492
00:17:49,367 --> 00:17:50,367
Huh?

493
00:17:51,667 --> 00:17:53,233
All together now.

494
00:17:53,633 --> 00:17:55,867
Happy Silver Anniversary!

495
00:17:55,967 --> 00:17:56,667
Huh?

496
00:17:56,767 --> 00:18:00,127
(Congratulations Goro-san and Towako-san)
(25th Wedding Anniversary) Congratulations!

497
00:18:02,133 --> 00:18:03,133
Here.

498
00:18:03,300 --> 00:18:04,300
So cute!

499
00:18:04,800 --> 00:18:05,800
Very handsome.

500
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:07,267
Looks great.

501
00:18:07,367 --> 00:18:08,367
Yeah.

502
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:11,567
Were you surprised?

503
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:13,833
Oh, my.

504
00:18:14,133 --> 00:18:17,233
Rio and Natsuki planned this for you.

505
00:18:17,333 --> 00:18:17,967
Yay!

506
00:18:18,067 --> 00:18:19,533
Rio and Natsuki?

507
00:18:19,633 --> 00:18:20,633
Yeah.

508
00:18:20,900 --> 00:18:23,367
They were worried you
two might get a divorce.

509
00:18:23,467 --> 00:18:26,233
After all, Towako-san
didn't tell us anything.

510
00:18:27,600 --> 00:18:29,767
I can't believe you prepared all this.

511
00:18:31,933 --> 00:18:33,300
Surprise!

512
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,067
A huge success!

513
00:18:40,033 --> 00:18:41,867
Surprise!

514
00:18:44,033 --> 00:18:46,267
Thank you, everyone.

515
00:18:46,367 --> 00:18:47,367
Really.

516
00:18:48,233 --> 00:18:49,600
Thank you all so much.

517
00:18:50,167 --> 00:18:51,233
Congratulations.

518
00:18:51,333 --> 00:18:53,100
Congratulations to you both.

519
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:55,067
Crying doesn't suit you.

520
00:18:55,167 --> 00:18:57,467
Oh, Yanagi-san.

521
00:18:57,567 --> 00:18:58,633
Teacher.

522
00:18:58,733 --> 00:19:01,200
What's a Silver Anniversary?

523
00:19:01,300 --> 00:19:04,700
It's an anniversary celebrating
25 years of marriage.

524
00:19:04,800 --> 00:19:05,700
Marriage?

525
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:07,133
25 years old?

526
00:19:07,233 --> 00:19:08,233
That's right.

527
00:19:08,633 --> 00:19:10,433
You're pretty smart, Riku.

528
00:19:11,033 --> 00:19:12,700
Right?

529
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:13,700
Good job.

530
00:19:13,800 --> 00:19:15,209
(Congratulations Goro-san and Towako-san)
(25th Wedding Anniversary)

531
00:19:15,233 --> 00:19:16,067
Huh?

532
00:19:16,167 --> 00:19:17,800
A hot spring trip?

533
00:19:17,900 --> 00:19:18,467
Yeah.

534
00:19:18,567 --> 00:19:21,700
Dad wanted to surprise you,
so he kept it a secret.

535
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:24,467
Huh, so that's why he's
been acting weird lately?

536
00:19:26,533 --> 00:19:28,367
Dad is terrible at lying.

537
00:19:28,467 --> 00:19:30,227
He made Mom suspect
he was having an affair.

538
00:19:30,300 --> 00:19:30,867
Huh?

539
00:19:30,967 --> 00:19:33,767
Weren't you the one who
said it might be an affair, Rio?

540
00:19:33,867 --> 00:19:34,433
Is that so?

541
00:19:34,533 --> 00:19:35,967
Geez.

542
00:19:36,067 --> 00:19:36,500
I did not.

543
00:19:36,600 --> 00:19:39,633
If only he were a little better at lying.

544
00:19:39,733 --> 00:19:44,067
But that's also part of
Takemiya-san's charm.

545
00:19:44,167 --> 00:19:45,167
Yeah.

546
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:47,700
And the reason he started
taking those classes was...

547
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:48,400
Fukuo.

548
00:19:48,500 --> 00:19:49,709
- Huh?
- Let's not talk about that.

549
00:19:49,733 --> 00:19:50,433
Huh, what is it?

550
00:19:50,533 --> 00:19:51,100
I want to know.

551
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:52,480
He originally took those classes

552
00:19:52,533 --> 00:19:55,100
to surprise her for
their Silver Anniversary.

553
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:55,967
Huh?

554
00:19:56,067 --> 00:19:58,933
Like surprising everyone
by playing the piano.

555
00:19:59,033 --> 00:20:00,643
- Huh?
- Or making a pair of matching bowls.

556
00:20:00,667 --> 00:20:01,967
That's so romantic.

557
00:20:02,067 --> 00:20:03,367
Not really.

558
00:20:03,467 --> 00:20:06,333
I have no talent for music or pottery.

559
00:20:06,433 --> 00:20:08,700
So in the end, I changed it to a trip.

560
00:20:08,800 --> 00:20:11,467
You're such a romantic.

561
00:20:13,500 --> 00:20:14,767
Honey.

562
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:16,600
Thank you.

563
00:20:17,233 --> 00:20:19,400
No, it's...

564
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:21,767
- It's nothing.
- He's blushing.

565
00:20:23,267 --> 00:20:24,000
Ah.

566
00:20:24,100 --> 00:20:25,100
- Huh?
- Oh, right.

567
00:20:26,033 --> 00:20:28,133
Let's capture this moment.

568
00:20:28,233 --> 00:20:30,000
- Oh.
- Yeah.

569
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:31,500
- Great.
- Nice.

570
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:33,133
I'll take the picture.

571
00:20:33,233 --> 00:20:35,033
No, Sota needs to be in it too.

572
00:20:35,133 --> 00:20:36,400
Then I'll take a selfie.

573
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:37,540
Get in the frame, So-chan.

574
00:20:37,667 --> 00:20:38,267
Huh?

575
00:20:38,367 --> 00:20:39,767
Ah, thanks.

576
00:20:39,867 --> 00:20:40,567
Is everyone ready?

577
00:20:40,667 --> 00:20:41,567
Rock, come here.

578
00:20:41,667 --> 00:20:42,533
- Riku too.
- Ready?

579
00:20:42,633 --> 00:20:44,667
- Over here, come on.
- Is everyone in?

580
00:20:44,767 --> 00:20:46,767
Rock.

581
00:20:46,867 --> 00:20:48,967
Say cheese!

582
00:20:51,033 --> 00:20:53,200
Oh, that was really fun.

583
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:56,100
So this is how everyone celebrates.

584
00:20:56,200 --> 00:20:57,767
It's so refreshing.

585
00:20:57,867 --> 00:20:58,467
Yeah.

586
00:20:58,567 --> 00:21:03,667
Doesn't your family celebrate
birthdays or anniversaries, So-chan?

587
00:21:03,767 --> 00:21:04,767
Well...

588
00:21:04,800 --> 00:21:08,533
We do go out to eat
with family and relatives,

589
00:21:08,633 --> 00:21:12,067
but we don't celebrate
together at home like this.

590
00:21:12,167 --> 00:21:14,000
Hmm, I see.

591
00:21:14,667 --> 00:21:16,167
It was a very warm

592
00:21:16,267 --> 00:21:18,433
and typical celebration for your family.

593
00:21:19,833 --> 00:21:20,833
You think so?

594
00:21:20,933 --> 00:21:21,933
Yeah.

595
00:21:22,267 --> 00:21:23,800
Thanks for inviting me.

596
00:21:25,400 --> 00:21:26,400
Yeah.

597
00:21:29,233 --> 00:21:30,233
Ah, but

598
00:21:30,333 --> 00:21:32,500
it was my sister who
said we should invite you.

599
00:21:32,600 --> 00:21:34,133
Ah, I see.

600
00:21:34,233 --> 00:21:35,233
Yeah.

601
00:21:35,367 --> 00:21:38,400
I actually felt a bit embarrassed...

602
00:21:38,967 --> 00:21:39,500
Hmm?

603
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:40,600
What did you say?

604
00:22:05,667 --> 00:22:06,467
Ah.

605
00:22:06,567 --> 00:22:08,033
Is this one wiped?

606
00:22:08,500 --> 00:22:09,333
Ah, yeah.

607
00:22:09,433 --> 00:22:11,100
Th-This one is already wiped.

608
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:12,240
- Yeah.
- Right, it's done.

609
00:22:12,267 --> 00:22:12,633
Yeah.

610
00:22:12,733 --> 00:22:14,433
Ah, can you help me with this?

611
00:22:14,533 --> 00:22:15,400
Yeah, sure.

612
00:22:15,500 --> 00:22:17,433
Then here you go.

613
00:22:17,533 --> 00:22:18,533
Yeah.

614
00:22:27,200 --> 00:22:28,667
I feel like.

615
00:22:29,933 --> 00:22:31,167
We're pretty good together.

616
00:22:34,267 --> 00:22:35,300
Oh, honey.

617
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:35,700
Yeah?

618
00:22:35,800 --> 00:22:37,767
Could you take these to Natsuki's room?

619
00:22:37,867 --> 00:22:38,533
Sure.

620
00:22:38,633 --> 00:22:40,933
Tell him to hurry up and take a shower.

621
00:22:41,033 --> 00:22:42,033
Got it.

622
00:22:46,133 --> 00:22:47,133
Natsuki.

623
00:23:11,633 --> 00:23:13,267
A summer storm...

624
00:23:17,367 --> 00:23:18,600
is about to hit.

625
00:23:18,700 --> 00:23:21,167
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

626
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:22,200
(Each family member's feelings and struggles)

627
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:24,600
Was math the only thing you came to like?

628
00:23:24,600 --> 00:23:25,900
Maybe it's time to end this.

629
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:27,400
Why are you so against it?!

630
00:23:27,400 --> 00:23:30,000
After all, anxiety always comes with love.

631
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:32,200
(A tearful decision made by the two—)
Because I love Na-chan's family...

632
00:23:32,300 --> 00:23:33,600
I don't want to ruin everything.

633
00:23:33,600 --> 00:23:36,100
Because I truly... fell in love with someone.

